From: hermes-i386 provisioning kit
Subject: [PATCH] main_tui_launch: clamp the V8 heap on 32-bit interpreters

V8 on ia32 cannot reserve a multi-GB heap within a 4 GB address space.
_resolve_tui_heap_mb() returns the 8192 MB default whenever no cgroup memory
limit is detected, so the TUI child aborts almost immediately with:

    FATAL ERROR: CALL_AND_RETRY_LAST Allocation failed
      - JavaScript heap out of memory

Note the failure signature: it dies at ~0.4 MB used, which indicates a failed
heap reservation rather than genuine memory exhaustion.

Clamp the default for 32-bit interpreters. Applied before the cgroup branch so
it also caps the floor path.

--- a/hermes_cli/main_tui_launch.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/main_tui_launch.py
@@ -654,6 +654,10 @@
     """V8 ``--max-old-space-size`` (MB) that fits the container: ``default_mb`` when unconstrained,
     else 75% of the cgroup limit (headroom for non-heap RSS + the gateway child), floored at
     1536MB when the container is > 2GB (below that V8 GC-thrashes)."""
+    # 32-bit (i386/armhf): V8 cannot reserve a multi-GB heap in a 4GB address
+    # space, so the 8192MB default aborts at startup with "Reached heap limit".
+    if sys.maxsize < 2 ** 32:
+        default_mb = min(default_mb, 700)
     limit = _read_cgroup_memory_limit()
     if not limit:
         return default_mb
